{"seq":22,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T02:27:40.609Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"1ed951e87db909802f40daef7e919b2c10fab66460b841f6b60ccdae6061b254","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"@Bettina, here's the list for Kwame's review. I pulled it from #coastal-team, #coastal-random, Moss's Coastal digests and cheat sheet, and your public 12/8 cutover recap. Pellow Home Living is left out. The share has no per-account ticket folders, so this comes from those sources only.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL)**\n- **#4419**: `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. Still open per Moss's cheat sheet.\n- **PD-8841**: Gate 4B double-booked chassis pool holds (your 12/8 recap).\n- **No ticket number**: CSV import bug on the Berth 2 yard map (your 12/8 recap).\n- **No ticket number**: chassis pool validation at Gate 4 during shift change, the main friction point (Moss's cheat sheet).\n- **No ticket number**: Gate 4B printer mapping (your 12/8 recap).\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF)**\n- **Feature request #882**: bulk-clear button for departed barges (Moss's cheat sheet).\n- **No ticket number**: tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B. Engineering gave the night dispatcher a manual CSV patch (Moss's cheat sheet).\n- **No ticket number**: patched manifest CSV requested before the 06:00 shift (Moss's 11/2 digest).\n\n**Needs checking**\n- **#4419 conflict**: the cheat sheet puts #4419 on PHL's report timeout, but Moss's 11/2 digest puts #4419 on a barge slip 7 schedule sync under \"Puget Sound Operations,\" which may be DMF. Only one can be right, so please confirm which account owns it.\n\n**Left out on purpose**\n- #8812 and PD-4821 (Pellow Home Living).\n- PD-4824 and PD-4827 (Saltmarsh Provisions)."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
